# Fairlead process settings. Copy to config\fairlead.env (git-ignored) and edit.
# Everything about providers, routes and keys is set once in the browser and saved to
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\Fairlead\fairlead.json (API keys there are DPAPI-protected for your Windows user).
# Variables already set in the environment win over this file.

# Gateway port. 8776 is Fairlead's registry port (docs/UNIFIED-UI.md); tools point at it, so keep it.
# FAIRLEAD_PORT=8776

# Fairlead listens on this machine only (127.0.0.1), a Fleet rule. There is no LAN option.

# 1 = stop when the admin tab closes (the TechStack default for apps that serve only their own UI).
# Fairlead serves other tools, so it keeps running unless this is set.
# FAIRLEAD_AUTO_STOP=0

# Where fairlead.json lives (default %LOCALAPPDATA%\Fairlead).
# FAIRLEAD_DATA_DIR=

# Cloud keys can also come from the environment instead of the setup page (the stored key wins):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# AI gateway (Responses API). Normally imported in the browser under Providers -> AI gateway, with the address entered
# there and the token kept in Lazarette. The settings below are for scripted setups.
# Default location: config\ai_gateway_models.yaml (git-ignored; see config\ai_gateway_models.example.yaml).
# Check it with: Import-Module .\module\Fairlead; Test-FairleadModelConfig
# FAIRLEAD_GATEWAY_CONFIG=config\ai_gateway_models.yaml
#
# The model file names the variables that hold the gateway address and token. Set them in your user environment or
# your deployment's secret injection, not in a committed file. The usual names:
# AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://approved-gateway.example
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=
# AI_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
